[#:seon.task{:name "the-hook-sends-only-forms-with-a-var-definition"
             :intent "The edit hook (bin/seon-hook, RF-4 at 3c15a3434) chooses the changed forms to send to the agent branch from clj-kondo's :var-definitions, so a changed defmethod and a changed top-level form that defines no var are never sent: the branch keeps running the old method, silently. The ns form is sent first when the branch lacks the namespace or holds other requires or aliases (not for changed refers, imports or docstring). Correct: every top-level form whose text changed is sent in file order. Proof: a seon.dev.hook-test deftest (to be written) editing a defmethod asserts it reaches the branch. Read `docs/seon/schedule/cards/RF-4.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "the-hook-cannot-load-a-host-only-test-namespace-on-a-branch"
             :intent "Editing test/my/test_check_test.clj (requires seon.test-support) with SEON_LANE=dogfood-fix-a sent the ns form and its deftest; the branch answered \"Unable to resolve symbol: support/reply\" and \"support/with-running-agent\" with :in-namespace {support []}: the alias exists but seon.test-support is not loaded in the branch's SCI world, so a deftest using the harness cannot run at the REPL (also seen in the dogfood pilot frictions). Correct: the hook (or the REPL) says the required namespace is host-only and names where its tests run (bin/lane commit --test), or the branch loads it. Proof: a seon.dev.hook-test deftest (to be written) asserting the reply names the unloadable namespace. Read `docs/seon/schedule/cards/RF-4.md`."}]
